CON-21: weight the summary averages by the routing step length

stats_updateNodeStats() added one sample per routing step to the node
depth, storage volume and outfall flow sums, statsrpt.c divided them by the
number of steps (ReportStepCount, or the number of flowing steps for an
outfall), and the pump average divided a sum of step flows by the number
of running steps. Under a variable routing step the steps are shortest
while flows are highest, so these "averages" over-weighted peak conditions.
Accumulate each value times the step length and divide by the time: the
reporting period (RoutingTimeSpan) for node depth and storage volume, and
the new OutfallStats.flowTime for the outfall's flow frequency and average
flow. The pump's average flow is its pumped volume over its running time.
The statistics getters of swmm5_stats.c divide the same way.

Requires: API-04
Requires: BND-19
Requires: BND-20

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after API-04_swmm530.patch, BND-19_swmm530.patch and BND-20_swmm530.patch:
    git apply CON-21_swmm530.patch

